diff --git a/docs/G1_HANDOFF_VENDOR_QUESTIONS_20260914.md b/docs/G1_HANDOFF_VENDOR_QUESTIONS_20260914.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..4eb7d70
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/G1_HANDOFF_VENDOR_QUESTIONS_20260914.md
@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+# Unitree G1 control handoff: support inquiry draft
+
+We need a supported transition from load-bearing Regular standing to a custom
+full-body controller and back, without an intervening zero-torque/passive phase.
+
+Observed on this G1:
+- Before takeover: CheckMode=ai, GetFsmId=501.
+- Custom controller uses ReleaseMode and direct rt/lowcmd.
+- After stopping its writer and SelectMode(ai), a later read-only query returned
+  CheckMode=ai and GetFsmId=0. The supported robot lost posture-holding torque.
+- This observation does not establish the exact instant or cause of FSM0.
+
+Please confirm:
+1. Which motion firmware versions support rt/user_lowcmd with API7110
+   SwitchToUserCtrl and API7111 SwitchToInternalCtrl?
+2. Can entry start from load-bearing Regular501, or must it start in PASSIVE1?
+3. Does LAST or WALKRUN restore load-bearing standing without a torque gap?
+   What command streaming/acknowledgement ordering is required?
+4. How are stale user commands, process exit and network loss handled?
+5. Which read-only API identifies the actual motion firmware and supported APIs?
+
+Installed SDK exposes these client methods, but server support is unknown.
+PC4 metadata: master_service1.0.0.2, patch1.0.0.4, video1.0.2.3, OTA1.1.0.3.
+These are not claimed to identify motion firmware.
+
+References:
+https://github.com/unitreerobotics/unitree_sdk2/blob/main/example/g1/high_level/g1_userctrl_dds_example.cpp
+https://unistore.unitree.com/manuals?slug=switch-sdk2
+
+Draft only. Not sent. Do not attach robot logs or identifiers without review.
